  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The ranking lists the largest federal contracts by total award value for FY2027 to date. The largest single contract holder is NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with a total award value of $43.5B. Lawrence Livermore National Security, LLC follows with $41.6B, and Consolidated Nuclear Security, LLC holds $34.7B. The Boeing Company appears at $22.7B, with Honeywell Federal Manufacturing & Technologies, LLC and UChicago Argonne, LLC each at $17.7B. Lockheed Martin Corp holds $15.6B. Mission Support & Test Services LLC, Maximus Federal Services, Inc., and California Institute of Technology round out the top ten at $7.7B, $3.3B, and $3B respectively. The page notes that total award value figures are full contract values, not single-year obligations. The summary total of obligated funds shown on the page is $43.5B.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors hold the largest total award values?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC tops the list with $43.5B. LAWRENCE LIVERMORE NATIONAL SECURITY, LLC and CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC hold $41.6B and $34.7B respectively. THE BOEING COMPANY, HONEYWELL FEDERAL MANUFACTURING & TECHNOLOGIES, LLC, UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC, and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP follow with $22.7B, $17.7B, $17.7B, and $15.6B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How do smaller organizations compare in total award value?",
        "body": "MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC has $7.7B in total award value, while MAXIMUS FEDERAL SERVICES, INC. and CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY have $3.3B and $3B. These figures are full contract values and are listed below the large national labs and major defense contractors. The list shows concentration of large total award values among a few contractors."
      }
